Vulkan: OUT_OF_DATE from AcquireNextTexture and QueuePresent is returned without an error report.

NRISwapChain.h documents OUT_OF_DATE as a result of AcquireNextTexture ("VK only: may return
OUT_OF_DATE"), NRIDescs.h describes it as the swap chain being out of date when
features.resizableSwapChain is not supported, and SwapChainDesc::scaling says the same for a
resize. It is the result a caller handles every time a window changes: recreate the swap chain
and carry on. SwapChainVK still runs VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR through
NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_VKRESULT, which reports Message::ERROR for every negative VkResult before
returning. A caller that treats reported errors as errors (a test harness, a debugger break in
AbortExecution, a log that fails a build) sees a failure on an ordinary resize, and cannot tell
it from a real one without matching message text.

This returns Result::OUT_OF_DATE for exactly VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR from AcquireNextImage2KHR
and QueuePresentKHR before the macro, without a report. The returned value is unchanged; every
other failure is reported as before. The validation layer passes both results through without a
report of its own, and D3D12 never returns OUT_OF_DATE from these calls, so nothing else changes.

Applies on top of NRI v190, independent of the other patches.

diff --git a/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp b/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp
index a879cb7e..d37cd106 100644
--- a/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/SwapChainVK.hpp
@@ -479,6 +479,11 @@ NRI_INLINE Result SwapChainVK::AcquireNextTexture(FenceVK& acquireSemaphore, uin
 
     const auto& vk = m_Device.GetDispatchTable();
     VkResult vkResult = vk.AcquireNextImage2KHR(m_Device, &acquireInfo, &m_TextureIndex);
+
+    // "OUT_OF_DATE" is an expected result (the window has changed), the caller recreates the swap chain. Not an error
+    if (vkResult == VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR)
+        return Result::OUT_OF_DATE;
+
     NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_VKRESULT(&m_Device, vkResult, "AcquireNextImage2KHR");
 
     textureIndex = m_TextureIndex;
@@ -526,6 +531,10 @@ NRI_INLINE Result SwapChainVK::Present(FenceVK& releaseSemaphore, uint64_t prese
     if ((m_Flags & SwapChainBits::ALLOW_LOW_LATENCY) && presentIdValue != 0)
         SetLatencyMarker(presentIdValue, (LatencyMarker)VK_LATENCY_MARKER_PRESENT_END_NV);
 
+    // "OUT_OF_DATE" is an expected result (the window has changed), the caller recreates the swap chain. Not an error
+    if (vkResult == VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR)
+        return Result::OUT_OF_DATE;
+
     NRI_RETURN_ON_BAD_VKRESULT(&m_Device, vkResult, "QueuePresentKHR");
 
     return Result::SUCCESS;
